From de69c76fecf5490c0fe151f4c451f35af7debfcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:43:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ui(casaray): apply the CasaRay theme per view

Frontend 20260930.3 (Core 2026.10.1) ignores a dashboard-level 'theme:'.
It applies only a view's own 'theme:' (hui-root passes
.theme=${view.theme} to hui-view-container, and LovelaceConfig has no
theme field). So all 28 views rendered in the viewer's profile theme.

Adds 'theme: CasaRay' to every view, the 7 subviews included, plus a
comment on the now-documentary top-level key. Purely additive: with the
28 keys removed, the parsed dashboard is identical to ha-deploy 18a4e5d.
No card, entity, path or link changes. scripts/ha_validate.sh passes.
Home Assistant 2026.10.1's loader reads 28 views, all themed.

Requires themes/deez_your_name.yaml (defines CasaRay) in /config/themes/.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jhp8H3KkTuJ1jpkMuSPTgR
---
 dashboards/casaray_v2.yaml | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

